---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro-expressive-code/components';
const cli =
  'cargo build -p cribra-cli\ntarget/debug/cribra scan examples/fixtures/inputs/credentials.env --format json';
const wasm = 'just wasm-production\nnode examples/wasm-runtime/scan.mjs';
---

<DocLayout
  title="Examples"
  description="Runnable repository examples, synthetic inputs, and explicit integration boundaries."
  back="/"
  backLabel="Cribra"
>
  <h2 id="rust-scanning">Rust scanning</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/Metalymph/cribra/blob/main/examples/scan_basic.rs">scan_basic.rs</a> builds
    custom rules, scans an ordered batch, and inspects finding metadata. Run <code
      >cargo run --example scan_basic</code
    >.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/Metalymph/cribra/blob/main/examples/query_results.rs"
      >query_results.rs</a
    > demonstrates finding queries and aggregate results. The <a href="/docs/getting-started/"
      >quick start</a
    > includes a short scanning excerpt.
  </p>
  <h2 id="transformations">Redaction and transformation</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/Metalymph/cribra/blob/main/examples/financial_review.rs"
      >financial_review.rs</a
    > composes current and opt-in financial catalogs, reviews synthetic PAN/IBAN findings, and creates
    a redacted derivative. Run <code>cargo run --example financial_review</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/Metalymph/cribra/blob/main/examples/share_safe.rs">share_safe.rs</a> builds
    a redacted Share Bundle. Transformations act on findings; candidates and undetected values may remain.
    Read <a href="/docs/transformations/">the transformation guide</a>.
  </p>
  <h2 id="cli">CLI</h2>
  <p>
    From the repository root, build the existing binary and scan a checked-in synthetic fixture:
  </p>
  <Code code={cli} lang="sh" />
  <p>
    The CLI accepts an explicit UTF-8 file or stdin and performs no directory traversal. Exit code 0
    includes finding-bearing scans. See the <a
      href="https://github.com/Metalymph/cribra/blob/main/docs/CLI_PARITY.md">CLI contract</a
    >; registry installation is not assumed.
  </p>
  <h2 id="webassembly">WebAssembly</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="https://github.com/Metalymph/cribra/tree/main/examples/wasm-browser"
      >browser example</a
    > scans and redacts caller-owned text locally. The <a
      href="https://github.com/Metalymph/cribra/tree/main/examples/wasm-runtime">runtime example</a
    > loads the same production artifact in Node.js, Bun, or Deno.
  </p>
  <Code code={wasm} lang="sh" />
  <p>
    These repository commands require the documented Rust WASM target, matching wasm-bindgen CLI,
    and Binaryen. The website does not bundle a scanner or build Rust/WASM. Follow each example's
    prerequisites and compare <a href="/bindings/#wasm">source and distribution coverage</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Built with Cribra</h2>
  <p>
    A future collection of applications and integration stories, added when their availability and
    use of Cribra can be verified.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
